clips.log
# Intermediates regenerated by inpaint.js and video.js on every run. The finished
# covers and clips are committed; these are the raw model output and the
# pre-band merge, and they are large, numerous and reproducible.
work/*-raw.png
work/*-merged.png
work/*-raw.mp4
work/band-check.png
work/*-noband.jpg

# Rendered output. Plan step 3.4, gate D3 ruled 2026-08-14: git holds the recipe, Storage holds
# what a machine publishes from. `png/<slug>/` is render.js output and is now published by
# publish-media.js to the Supabase `content` bucket; media-manifest.json IS committed and records
# the hash and URL of every published file, so what shipped stays provable without the bytes being
# in git. Binaries were 56% of history in three months with no video shot yet.
#
# The whole directory, not `png/*/`: the loose files at its top level are the pre-namespacing
# render output from before decks got their own subdirectory, and they are output just the same.
png/

# The publish set, written by render.js from png/<slug>/ plus the deck's cover video (plan step 3.4,
# completed 2026-08-17 when the rename moved upstream out of a manual copy). Every byte in here is a
# copy of something already on disk, selected and renamed by rule, so it is the most reproducible
# output in the directory and the least worth committing. media-manifest.json still records the hash
# and URL of everything that shipped, which is what keeps it provable without the bytes.
publish/

